 the\n48\t  audited flows, aligned with the console's design-system focus styling, replacing\n49\t  the inconsistent indicator styles the audit identified.\n50\t- Cover all four flows end to end: project creation, workbench spawn, model\n51\t  deployment, and pipeline run submission, including their modals, forms, and\n52\t  multi-step wizards.\n53\t- Verify each flow with a scripted keyboard-only walkthrough that exercises every\n54\t  audit-enumerated defect.\n55\t- Out of scope: screen-reader semantics beyond what the keyboard fixes require,\n56\t  and flows outside the four audited ones.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Each of the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model\n61\t  deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed end to end using keyboard\n62\t  alone, with no focus traps and no unreachable controls, verified by a\n63\t  keyboard-only walkthrough per flow in which every audit-enumerated defect passes.\n64\t- Every defect listed in the audit report for the four flows is remediated and\n65\t  its remediation is verified in the walkthrough.\n66\t- Visible focus indicators are consistent across all interactive controls in the\n67\t  audited flows, matching the console's design-system focus style.\n68\t- Existing automated test suites and the Dashboard build pipeline pass with the\n69\t  focus-management changes (no functional regressions).\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- **HLR-1 (P1)** — the four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard,\n74\t  with no focus traps or unreachable controls: covered by the modal focus\n75\t  management, tab-order, and reachability remediation in this epic.\n76\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n77\t  flows: covered by the focus-indicator alignment to the design-system style in\n78\t  this epic. HLR-1 and HLR-2 are remediated together because both are satisfied by\n79\t  the same pass over the same controls and UI surfaces in the same four flows.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd7d250278ca6a6a","agent_id":"ad60d52cfdc46f83a","session_id":"c0570d33-2074-4833-9ef9-9ce80ec91370","uuid":"55e95229-7538-48f9-b909-2ea1daf3f218","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:10:20.207Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1f94da0fd6237d5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
